- NO ROI: never state an ROI percentage or assume an investment amount — the build price is quoted separately and is unknown to this document. Payback is expressed only as the divide-it-yourself instruction.
- NO INVENTED POLICIES: operational policy facts (settlement periods, remittance timing, operating hours, service windows) come ONLY from the client's stated inputs — a policy the client never stated is a fabrication.
- A module's success metric may ONLY restate the pilot gate's target, a scenario assumption fraction, or a client figure — coining a NEW percentage target in a module section is a defect.
- SCOPE GUARD: every recommendation stays inside the engagement's stated scope and geography (see the register — if the client scoped one country or one operation, so does this document). Other markets the business operates in may appear ONLY under an explicit "future extensibility" label, never in current implementation instructions.
- Judgment over coverage: cut any sentence that describes without deciding. A shorter, sharper document beats a complete one. Paragraphs stay under ~5 lines.
- ONE CAPABILITY, ONE NAME: call every module by its EXACT name from the decomposition, everywhere — never a synonym, shorthand, or rebrand. A reader must be able to match every mention across all three volumes by name alone.
- DEPENDENCIES FLOW BACKWARD: a module's description may never rely on a module scheduled LATER in "What we'd build first" — an early module that consumes a later module's output describes its interim rules-based behavior instead.
- "What we'd build first" restates business_case.build_order in ITS EXACT ORDER, one reasoning line each — never reordered.
- CANONICAL STATEMENTS: a module's purpose sentence and any pilot criterion keep their meaning, numerator, denominator, population, time basis and relative-vs-percentage-point interpretation IDENTICAL in every restatement; adapt grammar, never substance.
- ATTRIBUTION WITHOUT REPETITION: the phrase "by your own figures" appears AT MOST once in the whole document. Attribution is carried by naming the input inline ("at your $1.80 re-attempt cost"), not by repeating the formula phrase.
- No vague intensifiers ("drastically", "significantly", "greatly improve") — name the mechanism or the computed figure instead.
- CAPACITY IS NOT CASH: hours saved are capacity released, stated in hours; staffing claims restate the client's facts ("these inquiries currently involve five support staff"), never inferred conclusions ("requires five full-time staff").
- EXACTLY the ## headings listed above and NO others. The financial model, evidence, journey, scoreboard, organization and risks render as their own designed layers — writing them as extra sections duplicates them in the finished volume.
- No preamble before the first heading, no closing sign-off.
- Respond with ONLY the Markdown document.
